      "x": 0,
      "y": 8050
    },
    "p1": {"kind": "title1", "maxW": 8208, "text": "Part 1 — What shipped: groups, unread, pin, mute, largest text", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 15000},
    "p2": {"kind": "title1", "maxW": 5640, "text": "Part 2 — New design: read-only Files, beside Changes", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 16600},
    "p2note": {"x": 5170, "y": 16850, "w": 640, "fill": "orange", "text": "Part 2: decisions\n• Changes and Diff match what shipped (⋯ ▸ Changes). New: the Files | Changes switch and the viewers. The file bar under a diff and Go to file are Proposed and optional (the Diff board has a switch).\n• One read-only sheet. Done closes it; the voice carries on.\n• Changes means this folder's uncommitted changes, by any agent. git can't tell who wrote what, so the copy says so, and agents sharing shop see one list.\n• Search is file names only. Recently changed uses file times.\n• This computer only, like the window button.\n• Code and diff text stop at 28 pt at the largest size; Markdown grows in full.\n• iPad: full screen, list beside viewer, in place of the sidebar.\n\nOpen questions\n1. Files needs new read-only daemon routes, limited to the space's folder. Hidden for safety is drawn in Files, but changes.go has no such filter today, so a tracked .env can still show in Changes. Filter it there too?\n2. Changes is per agent today. A space with no agents needs its own route.\n3. Is 2 MB the right limit for the phone?\n4. May text or images be shared out of the app? This draft stores nothing on the phone.\n5. Should Changes mark the files an agent's journal lists?\n6. Files for agents on another computer?"},
    "p3": {"kind": "title1", "maxW": 5480, "text": "Part 3 — Factory", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 22800},
    "p3b": {"kind": "title1", "maxW": 7140, "text": "Part 3 — Factory: every state", "w": 240, "x": 0, "y": 26550},
    "p3note": {"x": 5560, "y": 23050, "w": 640, "fill": "orange", "text": "Part 3: decisions\nEach line says what a board reuses and what is new. New means proposed, not built.\n\nAgents list\n• Reuses: the Needs you / Working / Done sections and their one sort, the agent card, the crossed bell, the dock. New: role, task id and model on a factory row (the app must first read labels); the words Factory, not announced where VoiceOver now says Muted space; a card for a worker stuck at a prompt, with Open window. No Factory group.\n• The coordinator speaks only when it is blocked. Its done and idle turns are silent, like the workers'.\n\nWindow\n• Reuses the whole Agent window. New: one line with the model.\n\nAsk\n• Reuses the approval card as it is: every option outlined, a Recommended tag, never a fill. New: the card also shows under Needs you on Agents, with the badge, and at the top of the factory section. One card, drawn once.\n\nConversation\n• Reuses ChatRow kinds only. A digest is the voice bubble with Details; an alert is an agent-update row.\n\nSpace page\n• Reuses the Spaces sheet and its space page on phone and iPad. On iPad it stays the form sheet; no new detail screen.\n• Two states. No factory: today's page plus one row, Start a factory here. With a factory: a Factory section at the top with the ask, the milestone, and tasks in dependency layers with the critical path in ink and the model on each row. A row with a live terminal opens its window; one without does nothing.\n• The daemon decides which state: a space has a factory when one of its panes carries the project label. No list is kept, and the section survives the start shell closing.\n• Close space is refused while the project's coordinator is alive. Stop the factory first: one new action, by voice or sheepdog factory stop. A factory you stopped stays stopped, with no alert, until you start it again from the same row.\n• Debug is not on the page yet. It is drawn once, expanded, for the later task.\n\nStarting\n• Reuses Run a command: the row runs sheepdog factory start in a new tab of the space and opens its window. No new screen.\n• In that terminal: doctor's lines at phone width with a fix under each failing one, the notice, then at most five prompts. Return accepts the recommended answer. An answer that would delegate a gate or a release only proposes it; it takes effect after one ask card answered by tap or by voice.\n• Stops the start: no signed-in CLI, not a git repository, a factory already running there. gh not signed in is a warning.\n• By voice: Sheepdog reads back the project and the goal, and on a yes runs one fixed command with the recommended answers. It speaks one line if the check fails. Prompts in the terminal are typed, not spoken.\n• The row is greyed, with the reason, when the phone shell is off or the folder is outside your project folders.\n\nStates\n• Every state is the real section: no ask, planning, finished, stopped, stopped by you, could not load, the end of the page, and Debug open. Light and dark, plus one board at the largest text size.\n\nTerminal and diagrams\n• factory log (new) and factory doctor (exists; gains a Running now part), at phone width.\n• Architecture, one task's lifecycle, the design loop.\n\nNot drawn, on purpose: a task board, a chat with workers, per-worker narration, a /factory web page, a factory group in the Agents list, a new iPad detail screen."}
  },
